- Yeah.

00:00:17.683 --> 00:00:21.240
- Just like an ax and I can
make a really good fire.

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:22.520
My father was an Eagle Scout.

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:23.420
- Oh, yeah.
- So like,

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:24.790
he taught us to make good fires

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:25.840
when we were younger.
- I love

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:27.180
that your first thing.
- But that's about it.

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:29.120
- You thought of was an ax.
(everyone laughing)

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:31.200
I was like, whatever Paul Bunyan.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:32.033
- I'm ready.
- I was like,

00:00:32.033 --> 00:00:33.700
you're like ready.
- Yeah! When I went camping,

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.127
I brought my ax.
- Yeah.

00:00:35.127 --> 00:00:36.760
- Yeah! I love an ax.
- I love it.

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:38.050
Okay, I love it.
(Chloe laughing)

00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:38.900
I have like, look,

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:41.260
I'm not even gonna own
how weird I am, nevermind.

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:43.340
- Go ahead! (laughs)
- I'm really into like,

00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:44.850
people used to make fun of me

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:47.070
